So my cousin says, yes, you are right. Let's go there.

We came up there. A hill, snow, cold, my God. How we went up there, God knows, to go to the village and go there, in the-- in the Ukraine is all locked in the windows.

They didn't believe that somebody survived. They knew that they're going to kill us all. I came to Milowce [NON-ENGLISH]. [PAUSES FOR 3 SECONDS] I opened the door.

To my horror, I'll never forget that picture as long as I live. An elderly woman was-- they hung an elderly woman, an elderly man, and her grandson. [PAUSES FOR 3 SECONDS] I became hysterical.

INT: Now where was-- where were these hanging bodies?

RK: From the ceiling in the camp.

INT: In one of the camp barracks, was that?

RK: There, it was not a barrack like we had. Because it truly was not enough space to build. It's a hill, like a tip. So it was like a stable. [PAUSES FOR 4 SECONDS]

