We were sent. I had to tell him something. We were sent from this camp to the other camp to work.

Ha, he says. You're lying. Where were you?

I said, telling you the truth. Do you have money? I said no.

I did have money. I had $6.00, 6 zlotys. You know what you could buy? Three eggs.

And my cousin says to me, give him. I said, I'm not going to give him. To him, it's nothing. He thinks we have gold. He thinks we have money. We didn't. We didn't even have nothing to wear.

Stop. We stopped. And, again, had all the-- I know that all the people were killed. I [INAUDIBLE] that they participated in it. Otherwise, they wouldn't know. And I said, we not-- we were in our barracks. We don't know anything.

