And they saw what those two fellows want to do us. They were dragging us. I didn't want to go.

And-- and-- and they start screaming. Why don't you leave them alone? Let them go. Let them go.

Once there's a witness, was a witness, they changed. I said, I told you. We don't have gold.

We come from a village. We had a piece of land. We worked very hard.

But we are Jewish. This is what happened to us. Please, let us go. They ran away.

I came to Lisowce. We went to sleep in the stable, because I was afraid to walk in-- straight into camp. There were a lot of-- tremendous-- a lot of German soldiers.

Among the German soldiers were Hungarian soldiers. [PAUSES FOR 3 SECONDS] But the Hungarian soldiers were not soldiers. They didn't have guns to fight. They had shovels to dig for them, for the Germans, trenches.

We went into the stable. And we lie down. And we-- we met some Jewish people, girls. She survived. She was in my house.

And I was-- and I met her in Israel, too. She says, do you remember? I was the first one to greet you. Greet me-- to-- to meet me.

And the-- the Hungarian-- they were there. Again, they put us to shovel snow, to shovel, to do something, not to sit for nothing. We didn't mind. At least, we are someplace with a lot of Jewish people. Whatever happens to them will happen to us.

For the Ukrainians, we were not afraid anymore. Because there were a lot of German soldiers. And there were Hungarian. And among the Hungarian soldiers were Jewish.

So we were not afraid. We stood there. I didn't remember how long. We did some things.

All of a sudden, we hear something very bad is happening. The Cossacks who escaped-- escaping with the-- with the Germans started to kill the Jewish people. I saw [? it ?] with my own eyes, cut off-- [INAUDIBLE] I told you before that we [? were in ?] [INAUDIBLE]. And-- and she had a baby. And-- and one [? aktia, ?] she covered the baby. Baby survived. And the second time, the baby was killed. This was the woman.

They cut her-- her neck off. And-- and-- and her husband's-- wounded him very badly, the Cossacks. I ran back. I ran away, back to tell everybody Cossacks are killing the Jews. [PAUSES FOR 4 SECONDS]

Meantime-- meantime, we couldn't do anything. What we did is one girl, ran to the Hungarians and the German soldiers to tell them what the Cossacks are doing.

